# Deny by default; nothing is tracked unless a rule below names it.
#
# The usual shape of this file is the opposite -- list the junk, let everything
# else through -- and that shape only works when you can enumerate the junk in
# advance. Inverted, a file nobody named simply does not get committed, and
# adding one to the release is a deliberate line in this file.
#
# Git will not look inside a directory it has ignored, so each one below is
# re-opened, its contents denied again, and then named back by glob. That keeps
# every glob scoped: the `!*.py` under a package can never reach into `build/`
# or `__pycache__/`, because those are never re-opened.

*

# ─── Root files ───
!/.gitignore
!/.pylintrc
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/pyproject.toml
!/pyrightconfig.json
!/requirements-dev.txt
!/run_tests.py
!/setup.cfg

# ─── .github/workflows/ ───
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
/.github/workflows/*
!/.github/workflows/*.yml

# ─── session_parsers/ ───
!/session_parsers/
/session_parsers/*
!/session_parsers/*.py

# ─── tests/ ───
!/tests/
/tests/*
!/tests/*.py
